class: abi
profiles: standard
summary: a C main installs its own SIGPIPE handler and then calls the argument initializer, which keeps it, since it ignores SIGPIPE only where it finds the default; a Landin write to a pipe nobody reads runs the handler once and fails with epipe, and a send on a platform/posix socket pair whose other end is closed fails with epipe without raising SIGPIPE
program: program.ldn
root: ../../../../..
c-sources: peer.c
status: 42
constructs: 0940, 1030, 1650, 1975
targets: linux-x86-64, linux-arm64, darwin-arm64, freebsd-x86-64, freebsd-arm64, linux-rv64
